This project has three PlatformIO test suites:

- test_native/       Host-only (no board needed). SystemState's isStale() and
                      BLETelemetryPacket's exact wire layout. Run with:
                        pio test -e native -f test_native

- test_can_protocol/ Host-only (no board needed). HondaCANModule's real UDS
                      protocol logic (request state machine, NRC handling,
                      ISO-TP frame checking, bus-off recovery) against
                      test/mocks/MockCanBus.h instead of real TWAI hardware.
                        pio test -e native -f test_can_protocol

- test_embedded/     Runs ON the ESP32-S3 board over USB (Unity output via
                      Serial). Requires the board connected.
                        pio test -e esp32-s3-devkitc-1

Run every native (no-hardware) suite at once with:
  pio test -e native

test/native_stubs/Arduino.h provides just enough of the Arduino API
(millis()/delay()/Serial/min()/max()) for the native platform to compile
SystemState.h, BLETelemetryPacket.h, and HondaCANModule.cpp unmodified.

More on PlatformIO Unit Testing:
https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
